At the Pale Dragon in Hamun, everyone was exhausted. Moka and Vera shared a bathhouse visit and spoke of family, loneliness, and the tower's visions.
Moka: Krill found me when I had nowhere else to go.
Vera: And your father?
Moka: A hero, my mother said. I want to meet him and prove I can stand beside him.
[end_timeline]
